2|6940||bib19|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1458483</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDonnell</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Beham</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sarkiss</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lo</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Importance of the Bcl-2 family in cell death regulation</article-title><source>Experentia</source><year>1996</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>1008</fpage><lpage>1017</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Experentia||52|1008||bib20|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miyashita</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Krajewski</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Krajewski</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tumor suppressor p53 is a regulator of bcl-2 and bax in gene expression in vitro and <italic>in vivo</italic></article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1994</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>1799</fpage><lpage>1805</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Oncogene||9|1799||bib21|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8183579</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>MRC: A report of the Medical Research Council Brain Tumour Working Party</collab></person-group><article-title>Prognostic factors for high grade malignant glioma: Development of a prognostic index</article-title><source>J Neuro-Oncol</source><year>1990</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Neuro-Oncol||9|47||bib22|'--></citation></ref><r